      "summary": "World Central Kitchen provides rapid meal distribution during natural disasters and humanitarian crises globally. In FY2024, the organization managed <cite id=\"3\">$327,840,221 in total revenue</cite> to execute its direct service feeding operations. The organization maintains strong financial efficiency, directing a <cite id=\"3\">90.3% program expense ratio</cite> toward program operations, which exceeds the industry standard of 75%. Additionally, it earned a <cite id=\"1\">100/100 rating from Charity Navigator</cite>. However, evaluation metrics indicate potential data anomalies in beneficiary tracking, alongside gaps in documented board governance transparency. While donors can support emergency feeding efforts via <cite id=\"5\">sadaqah and general giving</cite>, the organization lacks a dedicated zakat framework.",
